"""
The backend DuckDB of Mirco.SchluckiStore, as the opt-in module of that interface.

- A programme that wants DuckDB imports this module; one that does not never sees it, and its build holds
  no DuckDB and no C++.
- The five slots of Mirco.SchluckiStore are implemented here, so a call site names no backend of its own:
  openStore, createTable, scan, query, append and closeStore reach this module through the slots and
  nothing else.
- The database is opened with the safe layer of Mirco.Bindings.DuckDB: external access off, the
  configuration locked, no extension, no file but its own.
- A file of DuckDB is written by one programme at a time, and a reader beside a writer is refused; within
  a programme a second store of the same file shares its database.
- A column of a query is read only as the kind asked for; another type is refused, never converted.

    import Mirco.SchluckiStore.DuckDb (backendDuckDb);
    import Mirco.SchluckiStore (openStore, closeStore);
"""
import Mirco.SchluckiStore (
    StoreError,
    DuckHandles,
    cannotOpen,
    fileHeld,
    libraryTooOld,
    statementFailed,
    wrongColumns,
    wrongParameters
);
import Mirco.Schlucki (
    Table,
    Rows,
    rowCount,
    columnCount,
    columnKind,
    floatAt,
    intAt,
    textAt,
    boolAt,
    rowsFor,
    putFloat,
    putInt,
    putText,
    putBool,
    finishRows,
    destroyTable
);

module Mirco.SchluckiStore.DuckDb is
    """
    The backend DuckDB, the value openStore takes for a database of DuckDB; it is the same code
    Mirco.SchluckiStore gives.
    """
    function backendDuckDb(): Nat8
        ensures result = 2;

    """
    The database and the connection of an open file of DuckDB, both 0 when there is none, as the slot
    duckOpen of Mirco.SchluckiStore gives them.
    No contract: an Either result, which an ensures cannot look into; the answer is the work of the backend.
    """
    function openHandles(path: Span[Nat8, Static], writable: Bool): Either[StoreError, DuckHandles];

    """
    The rows of a statement of DuckDB, a column for each kind of kinds, read only as the kind asked for:
    another type is refused with wrongColumns and the column, never converted.
    No contract: an Either result, which an ensures cannot look into; sql is a literal, so no input of the programme reaches it.
    """
    generic [S: Region]
    function scanRows(connection: Nat64, sql: Span[Nat8, Static], kinds: Span[Nat8, S]): Either[StoreError, Rows];

    """
    The rows of t appended to the columns of sql through the Appender of DuckDB in one transaction, the
    count of rows appended; the first value, row or flush that fails rolls the transaction back, and
    nothing is written.
    No contract: an Either result, which an ensures cannot look into; sql is a literal, so no input of the programme reaches it.
    """
    generic [S: Region]
    function appendRows(connection: Nat64, sql: Span[Nat8, Static], t: &[Table, S]): Either[StoreError, Nat64];
end module.
